import orchestrate as team
team.JOBS={
 'hook-physics': '''Create ONLY dist/hook-physics.js. User wants real hooking similar to Raft rather than click-to-collect. Export class HookCast, constructor(T,{origin,target,maxRange=26,charge=1}), where origin/target are THREE.Vector3, charge is [0,1]. Constructor computes a throw destination toward target on horizontal water plane y=.05; actual range capped by 4+charge*(maxRange-4); target distance may be shorter. Projectile flies a visible parabolic arc to endpoint in .55 to 1.1 seconds. Class public fields: position THREE.Vector3, stage ('flying','floating','reeling','done'), caught (null or {id,token,type}), distance, tension [0,1]. update(dt,{hand,items,reeling=false,time=0}) advances: flight then floating; floating bob, drift gently with debris, find closest item within radius1.3 at landing or while floating, attach caught id/token; while reeling true move position toward hand at 8units/s, caught item visually follows position but DO NOT mutate items; when close hand (.7) sets done and update returns event {kind:'collected',id,token} exactly ONCE if caught token still exists, else {kind:'returned'}. If item token disappears after being caught, clear caught. If reeling stops, float/wait, never auto collect. Catch allowed during reeling as hook sweeps past item? yes but radius .75 so feels fair. Rope visual helper ropePoints(hand,segments=16) -> Array<Vector3> with slight sag proportional slack, and taut rope on reeling/caught; endpoints hand and position. Keep y>=water except shallow sag -.12. cancel() stage done. Avoid frame-dependent movement; clamp dt<=.05, update must not mutate hand, origin, target, items input. No scene, DOM, audio, material, randomness, external imports except T passed. No shell, git, deploy, or further agents. Include short comment integration example and full API. Coordinator handles charging, health, visual meshes, networking, costs. Only create hook-physics.js, do not edit game.js. Return concise summary.'''
}
team.launch()
